{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And Moses said to YHWH, See, You say to me</b> — This was on Mount Sinai, when he ascended there on the nineteenth of Tammuz, and Scripture had no need to say, 'And Moses went up to YHWH' and then 'and he said to Him, See, You say to me,' for whenever the Glory dwells on Mount Sinai, it is known that the [divine] Speech is there. And thus He said (Exodus 32:30), 'And now I will go up to YHWH,' and it says (Exodus 32:31), 'And Moses returned to YHWH' — he returned to the place where he had stood before the face of YHWH." "<b>Yet You have not made known to me whom You will send with me</b> — For You said to me, 'Behold, I send an angel' (Exodus 23:20), and this is not a 'making known,' for I take no pleasure in him — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Exodus 33:12). But this is not correct in the language of Scripture, and furthermore, for why would he say so now, when at the time that utterance was said to him he remained silent about it — would he now seek to gain relief on account of the matter of the calf? Rather, the matter is that the Holy One, blessed be He, said here to Moses (Exodus 33:2), <b>And I will send an angel before you</b>, and Moses said to Him: You have not made known to me who the angel is that You will send with me — whether he is the first angel, in whom Your name dwells. And this is the meaning of <b>And You have said, I have known you by name</b> — that You have made me known and exalted me by Your name. And thus R. Abraham [Ibn Ezra] wrote (Ibn Ezra on Exodus 33:21). According to his opinion, the angel whom they would choose is Michael. He understood with the goodness of his intellect from the verses that the first angel is acceptable to Moses and to Israel, but he could not know the truth, for he did not hear [it] nor did he prophesy [it]."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:20:44.922677336Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}